Bitmedia Labs is an international product company founded in 2014. Today, we’re a team of 150+ specialists working globally, building products used by millions worldwide.

Our work spans two core areas:

* Game Development — browser-first games for global audiences, centered on reward-driven progression and long-term engagement.
* Digital Advertising — high-performance advertising and affiliate platforms across Web2 and Web3 markets.

We are looking for a Junior Graphic Designer to create high-quality digital advertising creatives across our products. Your primary focus will be static, animated, and video banners, with opportunities to grow across Animation, Web Design, and AI-assisted creative production.

Responsibilities:
Create static advertising banners and other digital campaign creatives;
Create and adapt animated and video banners;
Adapt creatives across different advertising channels, placements, formats, and sizes;
Work with typography, imagery, graphics, and other visual assets to create clear and engaging advertising communication;
Maintain strong readability, visual hierarchy, and message clarity across different formats and sizes;
Create creative variations for testing and performance optimisation;
Work with brand guidelines and maintain visual consistency;
Explore references, competitors, trends, and visual approaches when needed;
Use AI tools to generate, edit, and enhance visual and video assets;
Iterate creatives based on feedback, audience needs, campaign goals, and available performance data;
Prepare production-ready assets according to technical and channel requirements;
Contribute to landing pages, presentations, and other visual communication materials when needed;
Keep design files and reusable assets organized;
Participate in Design Reviews and Critiques, provide and accept constructive feedback, share knowledge, and support teammates;
Plan and manage own workload, communicate progress and blockers, and work autonomously within agreed priorities and processes.

Requirements:
1+ years of commercial Graphic Design or Digital Design experience;
Portfolio demonstrating strong digital Graphic Design work, preferably including advertising or marketing creatives;
Good understanding of composition, typography, readability, visual hierarchy, color, and layout;
Ability to create clear and visually engaging advertising creatives;
Experience with Figma, Adobe Photoshop, Adobe Illustrator, or equivalent professional design tools;
Understanding of how creatives should be adapted across different digital formats, placements, and sizes;
Ability to work with brand guidelines and maintain visual consistency;
Attention to detail and visual quality;
Ability to accept feedback, iterate, and learn quickly;
Ability to communicate progress, blockers, and questions clearly;
Interest in developing skills across Animation, Web Design, and AI-assisted creative production;
English: B1+.

Nice to Have:
Experience creating advertising or performance marketing creatives;
Experience creating static, animated, or video banners;
Experience creating banners or advertising creatives for games or gaming products;
Experience working in a gaming company or on gaming products;
Experience with Google Web Designer or other HTML5 banner creation tools;
Experience with Adobe After Effects or other animation tools;
Experience with video editing;
Experience with landing page design;
Experience using AI image or video generation and editing tools;
Experience working with creative performance data, A/B testing, CTR, or conversion metrics;
Experience creating presentations or other marketing communication materials;
Basic illustration skills;
Education in Graphic Design, Visual Communication, or a related design field;
English: B2+.

Hiring process:

* Intro call with a Recruiter — Test task — Interview with the Hiring team — Сollection of recommendations — Offer.

Why join Bitmedia Labs?
We care about what we build — and about the people who build it. Our teams work closely together, share responsibility for the product, and support each other in everyday challenges.

As part of the team, you’ll have:

* Professional growth through products operating at global scale;
* The opportunity to experiment, bring ideas to life, and influence product decisions;
* Collaboration with strong, experienced teammates who value quality and teamwork.

We also support you with:

* Flexible schedule and the option to work remotely or from our hubs in Kyiv, Warsaw, and Berlin;
* Competitive compensation, regular performance reviews, paid vacation, sick leave, and public holidays;
* Modern Apple equipment and thoughtful corporate gifts for holidays and personal milestones;
* Support for your growth: courses, workshops, and conferences.

Through our charity foundation Bit Spilka, led by volunteers from our team, we support the military, medics, and civilians across Ukraine — delivering over $500,000 in aid to date. Here your work also drives social impact, and you can also join our volunteer initiatives.

If this resonates with you — send your CV and join us.
Let’s foster the world together!

