Hi there from Flatstudio! We are looking for a Graphic designer to join our team in Lisbon or remotely.

A few words about us
We’re Flatstudio, a user-centered digital design team. We make products that are efficient, enjoyable, and exciting for everyone. We're incredibly proud of the talented, respectful, and hard-working people who make up our crew. We cherish the relationships we've built and are always striving to create a positive and healthy work environment. Because let's face it, a happy team equals happy clients and happy users. That's just how we roll at Flatstudio!
Join our team! We are seeking for pro graphic designer ready to grow. Let's see if we're a match.

The Role
Drawing interface and illustrative icons in different styles;
Drawing illustrations and designing 3Ds;
Creating a visual identity for different brands – from scratch or rebranding;
Designing logo and handling the whole process from ideas to grid and guidelines;
Choosing brand colours, fonts and other essential features;
Creating extras for a brand – stationery, graphic elements, pitch deck templates;
Creating an explanatory brand book.

Requirements

Must-haves
A portfolio with at least 2 projects that include both logo production and visual guidelines or brandbook;
High proficiency in Adobe package;
Good skills in Figma;
At least one of the following languages: Ukrainian, English, Portuguese;
Ability to work under your initiative and autonomously;
Quick learner skills – ability to get a brief understanding of new areas/products in a short time and broaden it later as needed;
Practical experience using AI tools in design workflows;
A high level of attention to detail.

Nice-to-haves
Ability to draw sketches by hand;
Experience in Jira;

Working Conditions
Full-time and a schedule based on your/our timezones;
3 months of probation;
Salary based on interview results and extras based on performance;
Paid vacation (22 business days + holidays);
A cosy office in Lisbon, Parque Das Naçoes area with tea, coffee and a little bit of philosophical talks during the breaks (we are also okay with you working remotely full-time);
For office employees: employment contract, advanced medical care (Advancecare), city electric bikes (Gira).

Include your resume, portfolio, and a short message about yourself and your experience, along with your expected salary range.

